14. One important correction to the generated solution

I would not immediately build the final alert/dashboard around the exact metric names in that AI-generated response.

First verify all of these individually in your cluster:

vsphere_xcopy_volume_populator_progress
vsphere_xcopy_volume_populator_xcopy_used
vsphere_xcopy_volume_populator_source_disk_bytes
mtv_vsphere_xcopy_volume_populator_copy_duration_seconds
mtv_plan_alert_status
ALERTS{alertname="MigrationFailed"}

Especially verify whether the duration metric is actually called:

mtv_vsphere_xcopy_volume_populator_copy_duration_seconds

or has a different name in your MTV installation.

A good next step

Since you're already testing MTV migrations, run this single command first:

oc -n openshift-monitoring exec prometheus-k8s-0 -- \
  curl -sG 'http://localhost:9090/api/v1/label/__name__/values' \
  | jq -r '.data[]' | grep -Ei 'mtv|xcopy|migration'

That will give you all metric names currently known to Prometheus containing mtv, xcopy, or migration.

From that output, we can identify exactly which metrics your MTV installation exposes and then build the correct PromQL for ETA, stuck migration, throughput, failure, phase, and VM-size correlation rather than relying on potentially incorrect metric names.
